==German==

===Etymology===
From an older word {{m|de|lass|lass, laß|languid, slothful, idle, weary}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|laz||slow, sluggish}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*lataz||slow, weary}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*lad-||slow, weary}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|læt||slow, slack, lax, late}} ({{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|late}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌻𐌰𐍄𐍃||sluggish, weary}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|lassus||tired}}. More at [[late]].

